<title>THAILAND: Thailand extends land lease limit to 99 years.</title>
<headline>Thailand extends land lease limit to 99 years.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai cabinet on Tuesday approved a proposal to raise the limit for land leases to 99 years from 30 at present.</p>
<p>The government's move was part of its urgent policy to bolster the economy and revive the ailing property sector, the government said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The land leasing period of 99 years should be enough to boost investors' confidence for investing in big projects,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
